title: Suspicious Mass Process Termination
id: 69ac960b-f469-4463-b2d3-b4396bcff935
status: test
description: |
    Detects a burst of activity involving a single utility used for service/process termination, suggesting potential ransomware malicious activity.
    Ransomwares typically include lists of processes and services to be neutralized. They often attempt these actions without verifying their existence, which, through a loop over these lists, results in the creation of dozens of processes.
references:
    - https://research.checkpoint.com/2026/dfir-report-the-gentlemen/
author: Luc Génaux
date: 2026-04-28
tags:
    - attack.defense-evasion
    - attack.t1562.001
correlation:
  type: value_count
  rules:
    - proc_creation_win_taskkill_process_termination
    - proc_creation_win_powershell_process_termination
    - proc_creation_win_powershell_wmi_cmdlet_process_termination
    - proc_creation_win_wmic_process_termination
    - proc_creation_win_pskill_process_termination
  group-by:
    - Computer
    - Image
  timespan: 15m
  condition:
    gte: 10
    field: CommandLine
level: high